          <Pad Id="6CeydCsgnpGoSkaOYKunBU" Comment="Title" Bounds="192,1251,270,19" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="HowTo Draw a Bezier Curve with Handles">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="Qh3gsmHji9FEgyWW5KqD2C" Bounds="85,1380,1819,137" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xA;- The anchors and the ends of the handles are Point nodes (circle with Drag, defined in this patch) in two ForEach regions: drag them in the Renderer. The gray lines run from each anchor to its handle ends.&#xA;- Handles are relative to their anchor, in units: In/Out Handle = position of the handle end minus position of the anchor. Dragging an anchor leaves its handle ends where they are, so its handles change.&#xA;- Handle Modes is applied cyclically per anchor, an empty Spread means Free for all anchors. Change the entry or add entries to try Mirrored and Aligned.&#xA;- Mirrored ignores the In Handles, Aligned takes only their length. The In handle ends and lines always show the input, not the handles the curve really uses: with Mirrored or Aligned the curve follows the Out handles and the In handle is derived from them.&#xA;- Closed uses all four anchors with both handles. An open curve ignores the In handle of the first and the Out handle of the last anchor.&#xA;- The curve is one exact cubic per segment inside a QtPath, drawn with Path [Qt.Elements]. A path must fit one command to Qt (about 65 000 bytes), see HowTo Draw a Path.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <ControlPoint Id="GUmeXJUmtkvNAowxc5BSbz" Bounds="420,302" />
          <ControlPoint Id="NUwbWVWstdqMQdvxBzDimf" Bounds="112,253" />
